SWEET USB root disk RAM copy-on-write overlay (patch 0158, research 62 option 1): with rootrw=1 the driver of patch 0157 accepts writes into a bounded RAM block map (boot-arg usbrootcow=MiB, default 64, 1..512, 4 KiB blocks, ENOSPC at the cap); reads of written blocks come from RAM, the rest from the host; no write ever reaches the host (no new opcode). Without rootrw=1 the driver stays read-only. The whole pool (data blocks + hash table) is allocated once in ur_rootdev before any I/O, so the strategy path never allocates; allocation failure or any later ur_rootdev error frees it and leaves the root read-only. Applies on top of 0149. Unbuilt, untested on hardware.
